                "retweet_count": 1,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "50 years ago, Title IX opened the doors for women in athletics, but today we are still fighting for fair treatment and fair pay. In other professional sports, players receive around 50% of revenue from TV deals, tickets, sponsorships, and merchandise sales \u2013 WNBA players receive 0% of that revenue even though the value of the WNBA has more than doubled. I\u2019ve joined my @DemWomenCaucus colleagues to urge the WNBA to fairly negotiate with their players on contracts that reflect their hard work.",
